{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177017-need-help-designing-an-encounter","id":1177017,"title":"Need help designing an encounter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-18T12:15:26-08:00","id":1177017,"title":"Need help designing an encounter","content":"I am having a bit of trouble with the mechanical side of desiging encounters.<br /> <br /> The game is set in venice in 1208, they are tasked by their patron to go acquire a manuscript from a merchant. The merchant is supposed to supply the patron with interesting relic (ideally occult) and loot from the sack of constantinople in 1204. As a highlight the character also have to acquire a manuscript that supposedly contains a ritual that stopped the plague of justinien.<br /> The thing is the merchant was just eliminated by a hunter organisation in the city (the White masks) and were told that an important vampire would come.<br /> So we have one hunter posing as the merchant and a few others as workers in the building to keep appearances.<br /> <br /> The way i planned for the encounter is first the initiative goes to the players if they figure out something is wrong (either use of auspex or smelling a corpse in the room over) if not then the hunters get a surprise round.<br /> I have 4 players. 3 of them are good in a fight with one being more occult research focus.<br /> So what i plan is for 3 of them to hold off the hunters while one tries to find the manuscript. Maybe after a few round put the building on fire to add tension.<br /> <br /> So far i have 2 contingencies if things dont go according to plan.<br /> If the player just run at the start without trying to find the manuscript. The patron is very pissed and the player need to see if the hunters got the manuscript (they have). So then its a find the hunters and get the manuscript from them.<br /> If the player just lose the fight instead of being destroyed the hunters capture them to get information on their patron (their real target). Then i'll see what escape attempt the players try.<br /> <br /> That is all nice narratively but i'm having trouble figuring out the stats and mechanical developpement of the encounter.<br /> I'm also having trouble putting opposition strong enough to necessitate the use of willpower points but without completely overwhelming the characters.<br /> What is the average dice pool for a competent but not overwhelming attacker and how much defense do i give??? (so far I'm going with dice pool of 6 for anything fighting vampire related and a defense of 5)<br /> <br /> I am being a bit swamped with school work so i appreciate the help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 01-18-2018, 03:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T14:41:54-08:00","id":1177056,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know the strength of your players, so I can\u2019t speak to what exactly you should do. However I will tell you what I do. <br /> <br /> For 4 badguys <br /> Easy fight would be to give them 2 dice each to hit. <br /> Medium 4 dice<br /> Hard 6 or more. <br /> <br /> Adjust a little bit here or there. My players all have a defense 4-6 so. I go with the average of 5. And say a medium fight is 4 dice. So with the player that has 6 defense I am rolling 3 dice to shoot, and for the player with 4, I am rolling 5.<br /> <br /> Once you get the hang of it, it\u2019s super easy to just wing battles. Now if I am actually using a really nasty and meaningful baddy, I will actually draw them up and put merits in and all that, but most of the time it\u2019s not useful information. As a ST it just creates a huge amount of work for no return. Because neither the player nor the character will know if the npc had area of expertise in desert eagles or 3 dots of stunt driving ... ect <br /> <br /> Now for perceptions, stealths, defense things like that. I usually go with 4, 6, 8+ dice because the average dots a person has is 2 in stat and 2 in skill. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been DMing and STing for 15+ years. I know this method doesn\u2019t work for everyone, but my players generally don\u2019t complain. <br /> <br /> Though sometimes when they bitch at something like 10 defense... I\u2019ll just throw at them they have athletics, celerity, atavism or generally.. stop your whining and it\u2019s fine ^_~ <br /> <br /> Also in my years of running games, plan for your characters not doing what you think they will do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T19:49:10-08:00","id":1177139,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that is exactly what i was looking for<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177017-need-help-designing-an-encounter?p=1177056#post1177056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also in my years of running games, plan for your characters not doing what you think they will do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider this one of the great constant of the universe. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T22:12:13-08:00","id":1177775,"title":"","content":"I recommend creating a second encounter group, just in case.<br /> \u200bThis group would be a team of Occult thieves who are unrelated to the Vampires, instead interested in stealing relics from the Merchant's warehouse, possibly the contested scroll or just whatever happens to be lying around. They would also have more information on the supernatural then is healthy for your characters.<br /> \u200bIf your heroes find your first group too hard then the thieves could jump in, creating enough confusion for your heroes to at least escape.<br /> \u200bIf instead the first group is too easy then the thieves add fuel to the fire, making the encounter tougher.<br /> \u200bAlso, if your players decide to cut and run their disappointed patron could learn that the thieves now have the scroll and are willing to sell it, for a really steep price (or a five finger discount, honor among thieves and all that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T06:04:13-08:00","id":1178053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177017-need-help-designing-an-encounter?p=1177775#post1177775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend creating a second encounter group, just in case.<br /> \u200bThis group would be a team of Occult thieves who are unrelated to the Vampires, instead interested in stealing relics from the Merchant's warehouse, possibly the contested scroll or just whatever happens to be lying around. They would also have more information on the supernatural then is healthy for your characters.<br /> \u200bIf your heroes find your first group too hard then the thieves could jump in, creating enough confusion for your heroes to at least escape.<br /> \u200bIf instead the first group is too easy then the thieves add fuel to the fire, making the encounter tougher.<br /> \u200bAlso, if your players decide to cut and run their disappointed patron could learn that the thieves now have the scroll and are willing to sell it, for a really steep price (or a five finger discount, honor among thieves and all that).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a good suggestion, and if the players are smart and spend effort scouting ahead of time they have the potential to uncover the attempts by the thieves to case the warehouse, the hunter's presence and plans, and to determine several routes of entrance and escape--not all of which the other parties will be aware of. In all the chaos you are enabling, the PCs will do what you do not expect, up to and including surrendering to one side or the other. Count on it!<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T07:06:35-08:00","id":1178067,"title":"","content":"Sorry to say but the game was already played (last friday).<br /> The encounter went fairly well. Each player felt like they had something to do during the fight. With the character that was more mental having to search for the manuscript while the others were facing the hunters. <br /> They did feel that the fight took a long time, but to be fair none of them used their discipline. One character has nightmare at 2 and could've had one enemy simply made to run away. <br /> Oh well maybe that will teach them to read the book and learn their powers better... hopefully.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of two unrealted group going for the same relic as the players and i think i'll use that for the next relic they have to find. <br /> Altho this time i'll try to make an encounter that is less physical and more social.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}